T-005 mutation-resistance proof
================================

Procedure: for each mutation below, the production file was edited in
place (via a Python string-replace script, not a raw sed/patch, so the
exact substring boundaries are visible), the affected suite was run to
confirm it goes RED, and the file was then restored from a pre-mutation
copy and confirmed byte-identical via `diff -q`/sha256 before moving to the
next mutation. All seven mutations were applied and reverted sequentially
against the real repository files (never a scratch copy) -- `git status`
and `git diff` were checked clean of residue after each round-trip, and
the full six-suite set (facet-manifest-schema, facet-manifest-semantics,
capability-summary-schema, context-projection-schema, facet-manifest-
staleness, facet-manifest-parity) was re-run green on both runtimes after
the last mutation was reverted (see green-sh.log / green-ps1.log).

seq0763 evaluator remediation (2026-08-17) added Mutations 6-7 below, both
run AFTER the Critical/Major fixes that made them possible to catch at all:
Mutation 6 is the evaluator's own reproduction (CR injected into
validate-capability-summary.ps1) demonstrating the Critical fix -- the
.ps1 twin's process-capture mechanism was rewritten from PowerShell's
Start-Process -RedirectStandardOutput/-RedirectStandardError (confirmed,
empirically, to silently normalize CRLF -> LF and append a missing trailing
newline on the way into the capture file -- see "Critical fix evidence"
immediately below) to raw System.Diagnostics.Process + BaseStream.
CopyToAsync byte capture, and an explicit LF-only (no-CR-byte) assertion
was added to BOTH runtimes' parity suites. Mutation 7 demonstrates the
Major fix -- the provider-neutrality scan's "lambda" handling was changed
from a blind whole-term exclusion (which hid a real contamination string
identical in shape to Mutation 7 below) to an idiom-level mask that only
removes the literal `key=lambda` sort-key idiom, leaving every other
"lambda" occurrence (including a quoted string-literal assignment) fully
scannable.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Critical fix evidence -- Start-Process redirection silently normalizes
line endings (measured directly on this host, BEFORE any suite mutation)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
A child process was made to write exactly 8 raw bytes, `A\r\nB\nC\r\n`
(mixed CRLF/LF, no trailing newline after the final `\r\n`... actually
ending in `\r\n`) via `sys.stdout.buffer.write(...)` (no text-mode
translation on the writer's own side):

$ python3 -c 'import sys; sys.stdout.buffer.write(b"A\r\nB\nC\r\n")' | xxd
00000000: 410d 0a42 0a43 0d0a                      A..B.C..
(8 bytes, 2 CR bytes, confirmed via direct pipe capture -- ground truth)

Captured via the suite's OLD mechanism (PowerShell `Start-Process
-RedirectStandardOutput <file>`):
  byte count: 6
  bytes: 65,10,66,10,67,10                          (A\nB\nC\n -- BOTH CR
                                                       bytes silently
                                                       stripped)

Captured via the suite's NEW mechanism (`System.Diagnostics.Process` +
`StandardOutput.BaseStream` read into a byte buffer, no Start-Process):
  byte count: 8
  bytes: 65,13,10,66,10,67,13,10                     (A\r\nB\nC\r\n --
                                                       byte-for-byte
                                                       identical to the
                                                       ground truth)

This confirms the evaluator's Critical finding exactly as reported: the
OLD `.ps1` twin's own capture mechanism destroyed every CR byte before
this suite's byte-comparison ever ran, making the whole TEST-031 contract
(and the new LF-only assertion) structurally blind to a CRLF-emitting
`.ps1` wrapper on the runtime where it matters most (Windows, where the
staged CI's bash parity step is `if: runner.os != 'Windows'` and only the
`.ps1` twin runs at all).

